The '''Hi-Hat Café''' (Japanese: '''ハイハットカフェ''' ''Hi-Hat Café'') is a café owned by [[Pablo Millan]] in [[Ryme City]] in the game {{OBP|Detective Pikachu|video game}} and its sequel [[Detective Pikachu Returns]]. It is known for its coffee and live music.

In the original games, it is located on the first floor of a building south of [[Tahnti Park]], below the [[Baker Detective Agency]]. It is first visited at the end of Chapter 2. In the sequel, the café has moved to its own separate building west of {{DL|Ryme City|Fountain Plaza}}. It is noticeably larger, and has a proper stage for performing musicians. It is open from 10 am to 10 pm and is closed on Mondays<ref>Detective Pikachu Ryme City Guide</ref>.

